      "side": 1,
      "message": "I suppose I\u0027m a bit late in pointing this out, but it seems to me that in most of the places where the text \"hermetic\" appears, it\u0027d be more accurate to use the text \"embedded launcher\" (which is closer to what you put in your comment).\n\nThe latter clarifies that it describes the location of the launcher, whereas the former seems to claim that the entire process is hermetic (however, it\u0027s still possible to write non-hermetic programs even using an embedded launcher, for example, a test could attempt to access the network, or we might even want the embedded launcher itself to check a config file on disk for some reason).\n\nI\u0027m sure that all of the people involved at the moment know what you mean, but it seems to me that if it\u0027s not too hard to change it then it\u0027d be nice to give it a more accurate name.",
